insert into activities (id, lesson_id, position, type, concept, points, counts_toward_unlock, content) values
  ('b55f470e-4751-5981-9bb9-66893913e4ef', 'abc4d63a-7ff8-5b87-8697-901187822760', 1, 'content', 'what is AI', 0, true,
   '{"markdown":"## What is AI?\n\nBefore you read on, think: how do you think AI works? Can you name one place you have seen it?\n\n**Artificial intelligence (AI)** is a big field of computer science.\nAI systems are computer systems that do tasks like **recognizing patterns**, **understanding language**, or **making predictions**.\nThese are tasks that usually need human thinking.\n\n### How does AI learn?\n\nMany AI systems today learn from **examples**. This is called **machine learning**.\n\nFor example, to teach a computer to spot cats in photos, people show it thousands of photos labeled \"cat\" or \"not cat\".\nThe computer finds patterns in those examples. Then it uses the patterns to make a guess about a new photo it has never seen.\n\nNot every AI system uses machine learning, but many of the ones you use every day do.\n\n### Automatic does not mean AI\n\nA machine that does something by itself is not always AI.\nA basic calculator or light switch follows fixed instructions. It does the same thing every time and does not find patterns or make predictions.","title":"What is AI?"}'::jsonb)
