insert into activities (id, lesson_id, position, type, concept, points, counts_toward_unlock, content) values
  ('7200499d-b5f1-5ab1-83d2-994fe0d369cc', 'abc4d63a-7ff8-5b87-8697-901187822760', 6, 'content', 'AI limits', 0, true,
   '{"markdown":"## What can AI do, and where can it go wrong?\n\n### What AI is good at\n\n- **Finding patterns**, like spotting a cat in a photo\n- **Making predictions**, like guessing which movie you will like next\n- **Creating text or images**, like drafting a message from your prompt\n- **Understanding speech and language**, like a voice assistant answering a question\n\n### Try it in your head\n\nPick a task: recommending a movie, identifying a photo, or drafting a message. Ask yourself:\n\n1. What information would the AI need?\n2. What could it produce?\n3. Where could it make a mistake?\n\nA movie app needs to know what you watched before. It suggests new movies. It could be wrong if your little brother used your account!\n\n### Where AI can go wrong\n\n- It can state **wrong facts** in a confident voice.\n- It can be **unfair (biased)** if its examples were unfair.\n- It can **miss context** that a person would notice.\n- More data does not automatically make an AI better.\n\nBefore you trust an AI answer, check it with a trusted source, like a textbook, a teacher, or a reliable website.","title":"What can AI do, and where can it go wrong?"}'::jsonb)
