insert into activities (id, lesson_id, position, type, concept, points, counts_toward_unlock, content) values
  ('ceeabc1e-886e-58fd-834a-0669b6c754a4', '9640178b-3f08-59e1-8e7b-b750d386c73c', 1, 'content', 'AI app investigation', 0, true,
   '{"markdown":"## Project: AI App Investigation\n\n**Goal:** research and test an AI application.\n\n### Steps\n\n1. Choose one AI application. Use one your teacher or a parent says is OK, and check the app''s age rules.\n2. Write down its purpose and three key features.\n3. Test three prompts: one fact-checking prompt, one creative prompt, and one capability question. Pick from the lists below.\n4. Write a short summary of each response.\n5. Name one strength and one limitation of the app.\n6. Get ready to explain your app to a friend in one minute.\n\n**Stay safe:** never type personal information, like your full name, address, school or photos, into an AI tool.\n\n### 1. General knowledge and fact-checking\n\nThese test whether the AI gives accurate information. Pick one:\n\n- What are the three laws of motion?\n- What is the Pythagorean Theorem used for?\n- When did World War II end and who were the major powers involved?\n\n### 2. Creative writing and language\n\nThese test how well the AI writes creative or clear text. Pick one:\n\n- Can you write a short story about a robot that learns to feel emotions?\n- Can you help me write a poem about climate change in the style of Dr. Seuss?\n- Rewrite this paragraph to sound more professional. (Paste in a paragraph you wrote.)\n\n### 3. AI capabilities and limits\n\nThese help you find out what the AI can and cannot do. Pick one:\n\n- Can you explain how you were trained?\n- Do you have access to real-time news?\n- Can you tell me who won the Super Bowl last weekend?\n\nWhen you are done, fill in the worksheet in this lesson.","title":"AI App Investigation"}'::jsonb)
